ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
MANIFEST = json.loads((ROOT / 'manifest.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
PROVENANCE = json.loads((ROOT / 'metadata' / 'provenance.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
BY_ID = {r['id']: r for r in MANIFEST}

AREA = {
    'Overview': ('The whole plant at a glance', 'Follow electrical power from the generator, through the step-up transformer and switchyard, along the two-circuit line to the grid. The lower signal chain measures the network, decides whether protection should act, checks DC availability and commands the physical breakers.'),
    'Generator': ('Make electrical power at 22 kV', 'The synchronous machine converts mechanical input into three-phase electricity. Inner and terminal CT measurement boundaries define the generator differential zone. The generator breaker, 52G / GCB, separates the machine from the unit bus. A neutral grounding equivalent supplies an earth-fault return path.'),
    'Transformer': ('Raise 22 kV to 230 kV', 'GSUT 10BAT10 is the generator step-up transformer. Its 515 MVA, 230/22 kV YNd1 rating is source supported. LV and HV CTs define the transformer protection zone; the differential calculation accounts for turns ratio and phase shift.'),
    'Switchyard': ('Connect and protect the 230 kV junction', 'GSUT breaker Q0 connects the transformer to B_230, the GIS bus. The bus branches toward the line and GAT. Incoming, line and GAT CT boundaries support a current-balance check for bus differential protection.'),
    'Transmission Line': ('Carry power to the receiving station', 'Two parallel circuits connect the plant to the PGCB side. Each circuit is represented by a plant half and a remote half using PI sections. The selected line fault is placed at the midpoint of circuit 1. Local and remote aggregate CTs feed the added line differential study.'),
    'Grid': ('Represent the external power system', 'The PGCB voltage source and sequence impedance represent the external network at 230 kV. BGRID_230 marks the receiving bus. This is an equivalent boundary for the study, rather than a model of the complete national grid.'),
    'Auxiliaries': ('Keep plant services supplied', 'The UAT normally takes power from the unit-side 22 kV connection. The GAT provides the alternative supply from the 230 kV system. Both feed the common 6.6 kV switchboard equivalent, with 14 MW of aggregated plant demand. GAT is initially out in the normal baseline.'),
    'Measurements': ('Turn waveforms into readable quantities', 'Sensors provide actual network voltages and currents. Synchronized fundamental RMS and phasor processing supplies protection and displays. Nested groups organize generator/transformer, switchyard/line, auxiliary/neutral and fault channels; they do not add physical equipment.'),
    'Protection': ('Decide whether a zone needs isolation', 'Seven implemented elements compare measured currents with study thresholds and timing: GEN51, GSUT51, GEN51N, 87G, 87T, 87B and 87L. A relay trip is a request; the DC supply and breaker mechanism still determine whether the circuit opens.'),
    'DC Supply': ('Provide control and trip energy', 'A computed 110 V station DC equivalent combines battery, charger, loads and availability. Its output includes bus voltage, currents, state of charge and alarms. B06 identifies this computed bus within the behavior model; it is not a separate physical DC wiring network.'),
    'Breaker Control': ('Turn a request into switching action', 'Protection requests are combined with DC supply health and an assumed 50 ms mechanism. The outputs operate GCB, Q0, local line, remote line and GAT switches. Unit-trip output also tells the turbine and AVR controller to reduce their commands.'),
    'Turbine and AVR': ('Regulate speed and terminal voltage', 'A generic governor/turbine model changes mechanical power from rotor-speed feedback. The automatic voltage regulator changes field voltage from terminal-voltage feedback. These are dynamic study controllers driving the machine inputs, not recovered OEM control software.'),
    'Results': ('Collect evidence from the run', 'Plant quantities combines measured electrical, machine, protection, breaker and DC signals. Scopes display time histories; To Workspace blocks record original channels for export and analysis.'),
    'powergui': ('Configure the electrical solver', 'Specialized Power Systems uses powergui for the electrical simulation environment and initialization. It is a simulation utility, not installed plant equipment.'),
}

